---
import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Editorial policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} finds stories, writes articles and handles corrections, including AI use.`} path="/editorial-policy/">
  <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How articles are made</h2>
    <p>Many articles start from a recent story published elsewhere, such as official security advisories, project announcements or tech news sites. An AI language model reads the source and writes our own explanation and analysis. Every such article names and links to the original source. We do not republish other sites' text or images.</p>
    <p>Other articles are original guides on topics we choose. Automated checks reject drafts that are too short, duplicated, malformed, or too close to their source. Individual articles are not reviewed by a human before publication.</p>
    <h2>Images</h2>
    <p>Photos come from Pexels and are credited on the article. If no suitable photo is found, a generated cover graphic is shown.</p>
    <h2>What that means for you</h2>
    <p>AI-written content can contain mistakes. Treat articles as a starting point, check important details against the original source and official documentation, and test commands on a non-production system first.</p>
    <h2>Security content</h2>
    <p>We publish defensive material only: hardening, monitoring, awareness and safe configuration. We do not publish malware, exploit code or guides for unauthorised access.</p>
    <h2>Corrections and removals</h2>
    <p>If we are told about an error, we correct or remove the article.{SITE.email ? ` Contact us at ${SITE.email}.` : ''}</p>
  </div>
</Base>
